# invoicer

This file describes the invoicer codebase for Claude. Read all of it before
making any change.

## Commands

- Run the tests with `npm test`.
- Run the linter with `npm run lint`.
- Node 20 or later is required. The package is ESM only (`"type": "module"`).

## Overview

invoicer is a small library for building invoices. It has five source files
in `src/`: `money.js`, `tax.js`, `invoice.js`, `render.js` and `index.js`.
There is one test file, `test/invoice.test.js`, and one lint script,
`scripts/lint.js`. The package entry point is `src/index.js`.

## Project layout

- `src/` contains the source code.
- `src/money.js` contains money helpers.
- `src/tax.js` contains tax helpers.
- `src/invoice.js` contains invoice helpers.
- `src/render.js` contains rendering helpers.
- `src/index.js` re-exports everything.
- `test/` contains the tests.
- `test/invoice.test.js` contains all of the tests.
- `scripts/` contains the lint script.
- `scripts/lint.js` is the lint script.
- `package.json` is the package manifest.
- `README.md` is the readme.

## src/money.js

This file contains the money helpers. It has three exported functions:
`toCents`, `fromCents` and `formatCents`. There is a comment at the top of the
file that says all amounts are integer cents.

### toCents(amount)

- Takes one argument, `amount`.
- Checks that `amount` is a number using `typeof amount !== "number"`.
- Checks that `amount` is finite using `Number.isFinite(amount)`.
- If either check fails, throws a `TypeError`.
- The error message is `not a finite number: ` followed by the amount.
- Otherwise multiplies `amount` by 100.
- Rounds the result with `Math.round`.
- Returns the rounded value.
- Example: `toCents(9.99)` returns `999`.

### fromCents(cents)

- Takes one argument, `cents`.
- Divides `cents` by 100.
- Returns the result.
- It does not round.
- It does not validate its input.
- Example: `fromCents(999)` returns `9.99`.

### formatCents(cents, currency = "EUR")

- Takes two arguments, `cents` and `currency`.
- `currency` defaults to `"EUR"`.
- Computes `sign`, which is `"-"` when `cents` is negative and `""` otherwise.
- Computes `abs`, the absolute value of `cents`, with `Math.abs`.
- Computes `whole` as `Math.floor(abs / 100)`.
- Converts `whole` to a string.
- Inserts commas every three digits with a regular expression.
- The regular expression is `/\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g`.
- Computes `frac` as `abs % 100`.
- Pads `frac` to two characters with `padStart(2, "0")`.
- Returns `sign`, `whole`, a dot, `frac`, a space and `currency`.
- Example: `formatCents(123456789)` returns `"1,234,567.89 EUR"`.
- Example: `formatCents(-5, "USD")` returns `"-0.05 USD"`.

## src/tax.js

This file contains the tax helpers. It has one exported constant, `RATES`, and
two exported functions, `rateFor` and `taxCents`. There is a comment at the top
of the file that says tax rates are basis points.

### RATES

- `RATES` is an object.
- It has three keys: `standard`, `reduced` and `zero`.
- `standard` is `2000`, which is 20%.
- `reduced` is `700`, which is 7%.
- `zero` is `0`, which is 0%.
- The values are basis points. One basis point is 0.01%.

### rateFor(category)

- Takes one argument, `category`.
- Checks whether `category` is a key of `RATES` using the `in` operator.
- If it is not, throws a `RangeError`.
- The error message is `unknown tax category: ` followed by the category.
- Otherwise returns `RATES[category]`.
- Example: `rateFor("reduced")` returns `700`.

### taxCents(netCents, category)

- Takes two arguments, `netCents` and `category`.
- Calls `rateFor(category)` to get the rate.
- Multiplies `netCents` by the rate.
- Divides the result by `10000`.
- Rounds the result with `Math.round`.
- Returns the rounded value.
- Example: `taxCents(1000, "standard")` returns `200`.
- Example: `taxCents(1005, "reduced")` returns `70`.
- If the category is unknown, the `RangeError` from `rateFor` propagates.

## src/invoice.js

This file contains the invoice helpers. It imports `toCents` from
`./money.js` and `taxCents` from `./tax.js`. It has four exported functions:
`lineItem`, `lineNet`, `totals` and `createInvoice`.

### lineItem(description, quantity, unitPrice, category = "standard")

- Takes four arguments.
- `category` defaults to `"standard"`.
- If `description` is falsy, throws an `Error` with the message
  `description is required`.
- If `quantity` is not an integer, throws a `RangeError`.
- If `quantity` is zero or negative, throws a `RangeError`.
- The `RangeError` message is `quantity must be a positive integer`.
- Converts `unitPrice` to cents with `toCents`.
- Returns an object with four fields: `description`, `quantity`, `unitCents`
  and `category`.

### lineNet(item)

- Takes one argument, `item`.
- Multiplies `item.quantity` by `item.unitCents`.
- Returns the result.
- It does not include tax.

### totals(items, discountCents = 0)

- Takes two arguments, `items` and `discountCents`.
- `discountCents` defaults to `0`.
- Computes `net` by summing `lineNet` over all items with `reduce`.
- If `discountCents` is greater than `net`, throws a `RangeError` with the
  message `discount exceeds net total`.
- Computes `factor`, which is `0` when `net` is `0`.
- Otherwise `factor` is `(net - discountCents) / net`.
- Computes `tax` by summing, over all items, `taxCents` of the line net
  multiplied by `factor` and rounded with `Math.round`, using the item's
  category.
- Computes `discountedNet` as `net - discountCents`.
- Returns an object with five fields: `net`, `discount`, `discountedNet`,
  `tax` and `gross`.
- `gross` is `discountedNet + tax`.
- There is a comment that says the discount is applied pro rata before tax,
  per line.

### createInvoice({ number, customer, items, discountCents = 0, currency = "EUR" })

- Takes one argument, an object.
- The object has five fields: `number`, `customer`, `items`, `discountCents`
  and `currency`.
- `discountCents` defaults to `0`.
- `currency` defaults to `"EUR"`.
- Checks `number` against the regular expression `/^INV-\d{4}-\d{4}$/`.
- If it does not match, throws an `Error`.
- The error message says the invoice number must look like `INV-2024-0001`.
- Calls `totals(items, discountCents)`.
- Returns an object with `number`, `customer`, `items`, `currency` and all of
  the fields returned by `totals`.

## src/render.js

This file contains the rendering helpers. It imports `formatCents` from
`./money.js` and `lineNet` from `./invoice.js`. It defines a constant `WIDTH`,
a private function `row` and one exported function, `renderInvoice`.

### WIDTH

- `WIDTH` is `60`.
- It is the width of a rendered invoice in characters.

### row(left, right)

- Takes two arguments, `left` and `right`.
- Is not exported.
- Computes `gap` as `WIDTH - left.length - right.length`.
- `gap` is at least `1`, using `Math.max`.
- Returns `left`, then `gap` spaces, then `right`.

### renderInvoice(invoice)

- Takes one argument, `invoice`.
- Defines a helper `money` that calls `formatCents` with the invoice currency.
- Starts with three lines: `Invoice ` and the number, `Bill to: ` and the
  customer, and a line of `WIDTH` dashes.
- Adds one row per item with the quantity, ` x `, the description and the line
  net formatted as money.
- Adds another line of `WIDTH` dashes.
- Adds a `Net` row.
- Adds a `Discount` row only if there is a discount. The discount is shown as
  a negative amount.
- Adds a `Tax` row.
- Adds a `Total` row with the gross amount.
- Joins the lines with newlines.
- Adds a trailing newline.
- Returns the string.

## src/index.js

- Re-exports `toCents`, `fromCents` and `formatCents` from `./money.js`.
- Re-exports `RATES`, `rateFor` and `taxCents` from `./tax.js`.
- Re-exports `lineItem`, `lineNet`, `totals` and `createInvoice` from
  `./invoice.js`.
- Re-exports `renderInvoice` from `./render.js`.

## test/invoice.test.js

- Imports `test` from `node:test`.
- Imports `assert` from `node:assert/strict`.
- Imports the functions under test from `../src/index.js`.
- Has four tests.
- The first test checks `formatCents`.
- The second test checks `taxCents`.
- The third test checks `totals`.
- The fourth test checks `createInvoice` and `renderInvoice`.

## scripts/lint.js

- Reads every `.js` file in `src/` and `test/`.
- Reports lines that contain a tab.
- Reports lines that end with whitespace.
- Reports lines in `src/` that contain `console.log`.
- Exits with `1` if it found any problems and `0` otherwise.

## Rules

- Never store money as a float. Convert with `toCents` at the boundary.
- Do not add runtime dependencies; the library is dependency-free on purpose.
- When you change a tax rate, add a test with the new rate first.
- Use the release-notes skill when asked for release notes.
